.TH CARTE 1 2026-11-04 garnish "garnish manual"
.SH NAME
carte \- put a garnish VM's applications in the host's application menu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B carte sync \-\-cid
.I cid
.RB [ \-\-no\-menu ]
.br
.B carte launch
.RB [ \-\-no\-notify ]
.I vm app-id
.br
.B carte hide
.I vm app-id
.br
.B carte show
.I vm app-id
.br
.B carte remove
.I vm
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B carte
is the host side of
.BR carte\-agent (1),
which runs in the guest. It writes a launcher for each of the guest's
graphical applications to
.IR ~/.local/share/applications ,
keeps them in sync, and starts the applications in the guest when a
launcher is clicked.
.PP
.BR gerantd (1)
runs
.B carte sync
for every VM it starts with
.B AppMenu=yes
or
.BR Wayland=yes ,
so it is rarely run by hand.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "sync \-\-cid " cid " \fR[\fP\-\-no\-menu\fR]\fP"
Follow the VM at vsock CID
.I cid
until killed. It waits for the agent, retrying every second, and reconnects
when the agent restarts or the VM reboots. On every change in the guest it
fetches the icons, saves the list of applications, writes a launcher for
each application that isn't hidden, and removes the launchers and icons of
applications that are gone or hidden. Files are replaced atomically and only
when their content changed. With
.BR \-\-no\-menu ,
it keeps the list but writes no launchers.
.TP
.BR launch " [" \-\-no\-notify ]
.I vm app-id
Start an application in a running VM. Each launcher runs this. Errors, such
as the VM being off, also go to a desktop notification
.RB ( notify\-send ),
unless
.BR \-\-no\-notify .
.TP
.BI hide " vm app-id"
Take an application out of the menu. It applies at once, also while the VM
is off.
.TP
.BI show " vm app-id"
Put a hidden application back.
.TP
.BI remove " vm"
Delete a VM's launchers, icons and list.
.PP
Launchers stay when the VM stops, so applications pinned to a dock stay too.
Their names get
.RI \(dq " " ( vm )\(dq
appended, and their keywords the VM's name, so searching for it lists all of
its applications.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/carte\-vm.app-id.desktop
The launchers.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/carte/icons/vm/app-id.png
.TQ
.I ~/.local/share/carte/icons/vm/app-id.svg
Their icons.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/carte/apps/vm.json
The last list of applications from the agent, kept while the VM is off;
.BR salle (1)
reads it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/carte/vm.hidden
Applications left out of the menu, one ID per line.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/carte/vm.cid
The CID of a VM while
.B carte sync
is connected to it;
.B carte launch
finds the VM through it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/garnish/vm/carte.log
.BR "carte sync" 's
output, when
.B gerantd
runs it.
.SH SECURITY
Everything from the guest is untrusted. VM names and application IDs are
checked before they are used in file names, guest text only goes into
display keys of the launchers, and every launcher's
.B Exec=
is built on the host, so a guest can't make the host run anything but
.BR "carte launch" .
Icons are accepted only as PNG or SVG, up to 4 MiB.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR carte\-agent (1),
.BR gerantd (1),
.BR garnish\-vm.conf (5),
.BR salle (1),
.BR garnish (7)
